# F-16C Block 52 — the combining glass, declared.
# Format: doc/render/hud-declaration.md. This file replaces sim/src/modules/f16/displays/FBF16Hud.cpp
# and every number in it is that file's number, with that file's source.
#
# THE CUT IS THE OWNER'S AND IT STANDS: THIS GLASS CARRIES TARGETING ONLY. No horizon, no pitch
# ladder, no heading/speed/altitude band, no steerpoint diamond — those live in the MFD bank below the
# windscreen. What remains, remains for a reason:
#   cross     where the NOSE points, i.e. where the barrel points — the aiming reference itself
#   fpm       not a flight instrument here but the DATUM the fall line hangs on
#   contacts  every radar echo at its own world az/el; the locked one as the primary TD box
#   ccip      where the bomb LANDS, with its fall line and release cue
#   funnel    the EEGS lead solution with its wingspan walls
#   dlz       Rmin/Rtr/Raero and the target's range inside them
#   one line  the selected weapon, and the shoot cue
#
# THE TWO PROJECTORS ARE THE SEMANTICS. `frame world` = the scene's own camera basis, so the symbol
# sits on the thing it means (conformal). `frame body`/`screen` = straight onto the glass, because the
# glass IS the aircraft's system and rolling a lead solution with the horizon would be a lie.

hud f16
scale 1.9              # [SET] symbol pixel scale; symbols do not grow with the window
color 0.30 1.00 0.40   # MIL-STD-1787 monochrome green
inset 10
# The combiner's total field of view [DOC doc/modules/f16/hud-symbology.md]. Positions stay conformal;
# only symbol SIZE is scaled by 60/25, because a symbol drawn at true angular size in a 60 deg scene
# projection appears 2.4x smaller than the pilot sees it through the glass.
tfov 25

text x 0.5 y 0 dy 30 align c size 3 text "NO TELEMETRY" color 1.0 0.8 0.2 when !telemetry

# ---- the aiming reference: the gun boresight cross, screen-fixed, always there.
# 6.4 / 17.8 mR are the predecessor's 5 / 14 scaled pixels at this deck's scale and this projector
# (1.496 px/mR at 720p), carried over rather than re-invented.
cross x 0.5 y 0.5 gap 6.4 len 17.8

# ---- the flight path marker. [BMS-34 p.108] "a 10 mR circle with 10 mR wings ... along with a 5 mR
# tail" — diameter 10, wings 10 each, tail 5 UP.
fpm size 10 len 10 size2 5

# ---- the radar contacts as target marks. [BMS-34 p.109] "the Primary TD-box measures 25 mR on each
# side ... the Secondary TD-boxes ... are 15 mR". Off the glass they become the target locator line:
# [BMS-34 pp.104,109] "40 mR dotted line from the gun boresight cross ... F = FCR + 2-digit angle".
# A contact carries NO identity, so no box is labelled with a side — only the IFF reply is drawn.
contacts size 25 size2 15 len 40 fmt "%4.1f"

# ---- CCIP. [BMS-34 p.625] "1 mR dot at the centre of a 12 mR circle"; the 16 mR ring is the in-range
# cue and is a STATEMENT, not decoration. 5 s full-scale release bar [SET].
ccip size 12 size2 16 count 9 span 5 when ag_valid

# ---- the EEGS funnel: walls = the target's wingspan at the range the gun is aimed for, so
# "out of range" is literally span < bottom width and never a second rule.
funnel h 46 size 7.6 when gun_valid

# ---- the DLZ bracket, right of the sight: Rmin .. Raero bottom to top, the target range as the
# pointer, Rtr as the dashed cross-bar.
dlz x 0.5 dx 118 h 116 w 10 fmt "%4.1f" when dlz_valid

# ---- the one text line: what is being shot with, and whether now.
text x 0 dx 11 y 1 dy -15 size 1.15 fmt "GUN %4.0f" src gun_rounds when gun_ready
text x 0 dx 95 y 1 dy -15 size 1.15 fmt "STA %1.0f" src station when station_selected

text x 0.5 y 0.5 dy 40 align c size 1.15 text "SHOOT" when gun_in_funnel
text x 0.5 y 0.5 dy 40 align c size 1.15 text "SHOOT" when in_zone
text x 0.5 y 0.5 dy 40 align c size 1.15 text "RELEASE" when ag_release
text x 0.5 y 0.5 dy 54 align c size 1.15 text "IN RANGE" when dlz_valid
